Package: mosaicresid
Type: Package
Title: Residual-Shaded Mosaic Plots for 'ggplot2'
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Your", "Name", email = "you@example.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A 'ggplot2'-native alternative to base R's mosaicplot(shade = TRUE).
    geom_mosaic_residual() takes two categorical variables mapped the same way
    as any other 'ggplot2' geom, aes(x =, y =), recursively partitions the
    unit square into tiles sized by their joint proportions (true mosaic-plot
    geometry, not a heuristic approximation), computes Pearson (or deviance,
    or Freeman-Tukey) residuals against a two-way independence model, and maps
    the residual to fill color -- all automatically, as part of the stat, with
    no manual computation required from the end user. Works on raw
    (one-row-per-observation) or pre-aggregated (contingency-table) data
    through the same code path, and the computed rectangle/residual table is
    itself available as a tidy data frame via compute_mosaic_residuals().
